---
#2461: fenced `bynk` examples in a doc comment are type-checked by `bynk test`,
as cases in a synthetic suite on this unit. They are not run, so the run below
reports only the real suite's case.

```bynk
expect double(2) == 4
```

An example opts out with `ignore`, and a fence in another language is left
alone.

```bynk ignore
double(...)
```

```ts
const four: number = double(2);
```
---
commons demo.calc

---
Doubles a number.

```bynk
let four = double(2)
expect four == 4
```
---
fn double(n: Int) -> Int {
  n * 2
}
